Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.740 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Mass Effect Andromeda is on the horizon  and yes I am totally proud of that pun  the new space adventure is looking to be  pretty different from the original  trilogy a new galaxy means we'll be  exploring new planets with new aliens  using new powers and weapons here are  seven big changes you can look forward  to when the game launches number one  piloting the tempest shepard had the  Normandy in the original trilogy but the  riders siblings command the new Tempest  this time around I'm sure you remember  gliding around that miniature galaxy map  if only because of that awesome music  and flying around Andromeda is similar  only this time you'll stand on the  bridge of your ship and gaze out at the  Stars to choose your destination  the trade-off Bioware has said there  will be no loading screens from ship to  planet making your trips totally  seamless number two new and returning  species so when you step off the tempest  on these new planets what sort of alien  species can you expect to see well  you'll have a Krogan named Drac a turian  named veteran and an asari named PB and  your party as four new species Bioware  has already given us a sneak peek at the  evil ket we'll also be going up against  the remnants whatever they are in the  name of another new race called the  Angora has also been spotted the studio  also said that not all races are  returning in Andromeda and considering  the new setting  I wouldn't expect to see any keepers  from the Citadel but fingers crossed for  some Elcor number three exploring the  Nexus speaking of the Citadel it's gone  your new home away from home is the  Nexus which has been called a more  streamlined version of the old hub world  despite its smaller size it still packs  an archived history of the galaxy's  security centres science lab and  off-duty lounge some sort of Nexus level  can also be seen in the game's Paul's  menu so perhaps upgrading the hub world  opens up more planets to explore number  four resource mining and crafting  while you're cruising around those  planets in the Nomad be on the lookout  for resources Andromeda has new mining  and crafting options for weapons and  armor you'll find blueprints throughout  the game that you can use to upgrade  your gear and your new scanner can  collect minerals from various sources  these are then funneled into mods and  improvements for your loadout number  five more mobile combat of course not  everything on these planets is going to  play nice Bioware has said that the  game's combat is more mobile this time  around and it shows biotic charges can  be combined with jetpack boosts to shoot  all around the battlefield stunning  enemies in your path we've also seen a  sort of biotic shield in action which is  much more mobile than a previous games  bubble shield the developers have also  commented on finding that balance  between RPG and FPS gameplay and these  changes to combat seem to be working in  their favor  number 6 environmental hazards you see  it's not just hostile troops you have to  watch out for Andromeda also has a  variety of environmental hazards we've  seen a heat meter in the gameplay videos  so odds are we'll have to watch out for  extremely cold and poisonous  environments as well  random giant creatures can also attack  the party while exploring so you won't  be able to just trot around the surface  all willy-nilly number 7 loyalty  missions and side activities so you can  mine for resources and fight enemies on  the new planets what else  well foil T missions are back and so are  those steamy romance options but this  time they're not tied to the story  they're more like side quests and you  can complete them even after you finish  the campaign other side activities  include clearing enemy bases and those  are a bit more story centric Bioware  says taking these on won't be easy as  the bases are loaded with tough enemy  forces and plenty of alarms to let them  know that writer and the party have  arrived  Mass Effect Andromeda doesn't have a  solid release date yet but we know it's  coming to ps4 Xbox one and PC in spring  2017 Mass Effect 3 launched in 2012 so  Bioware has had plenty of time to make  changes to the franchise over almost 5  years which change excites you the most  is it one we missed let us know in the  comments and check out our ex  pensive breakdown of the latest gameplay  trailer while you're at it for all the  Mass Effect Andromeda coverage you need  you're already in the right place  you

